ROCm 7.2.4: preserve graph identity under concurrent construction.

GraphNode::nextID was incremented without synchronization before nodeSetLock_
was acquired. Independent TP graph builders can therefore allocate duplicate
IDs, including duplicates within one graph after a lost counter update.
The packet scheduler used that diagnostic ID for its visited set, silently
omitting nodes and dependent paths while graph launch still returned success.

Use object identity for scheduling and relaxed atomic counters for labels.
No graph capture, packet batching, concurrency, or inference policy is disabled.
Covered by V2_Integration_HIPConcurrentGraphIdentity in ProductionParityPreflight.

